# 🟢 Level 1 – Beginner Explanation

# What is Cloud Computing?

Cloud computing means **using computing resources (servers, storage, databases, networking, software) over the internet instead of owning physical hardware**.

Instead of buying your own server, you rent computing power from a cloud provider.

---

## 🏠 Real-Life Analogy

Imagine electricity.

Years ago:

Every company needed its own generator.

Today:

Everyone uses electricity from the power grid.

Cloud computing works similarly.

Instead of buying servers:

You rent computing resources whenever you need them.

---

# Traditional vs Cloud

### Traditional

```text
Company

↓

Own Servers

↓

Own Storage

↓

Own Maintenance
```

---

### Cloud

```text
Company

↓

AWS / Azure / GCP

↓

Pay for Usage
```

---

