# 🟡 Level 2 – Cloud Service Models

# IaaS (Infrastructure as a Service)

Cloud provider supplies:

* Virtual Machines
* Storage
* Networking

Customer manages:

* Operating System
* Applications
* Security configuration
* Data

Examples:

* Amazon EC2
* Azure Virtual Machines
* Google Compute Engine

---

# PaaS (Platform as a Service)

Cloud provider manages:

* Infrastructure
* Operating System
* Runtime

Customer manages:

* Application
* Data

Examples:

* Azure App Service
* Google App Engine
* AWS Elastic Beanstalk

---

# SaaS (Software as a Service)

Everything is managed by the provider.

Users simply use the application.

Examples:

* Microsoft 365
* Gmail
* Salesforce
* Dropbox

---

# Comparison

| Model | You Manage           | Provider Manages     |
| ----- | -------------------- | -------------------- |
| IaaS  | OS, Apps, Data       | Hardware, Networking |
| PaaS  | Apps, Data           | Infrastructure + OS  |
| SaaS  | User Settings & Data | Everything else      |

---

# Deployment Models

## Public Cloud

Shared infrastructure.

Examples:

* AWS
* Azure
* GCP

---

## Private Cloud

Dedicated infrastructure for one organization.

Used by:

* Banks
* Governments
* Defense organizations

---

## Hybrid Cloud

Combination of:

Private Cloud

*

Public Cloud

Many enterprises use this approach.

---

# Multi-Cloud

Using more than one cloud provider.

Example:

AWS

*

Azure

*

Google Cloud

